{"pageProps":{"note":{"id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","title":"Forensic evidence photography — reference scales","desc":"Crime-scene photography's L-shaped reference scale, and a NIST-adjacent study finding the standard isn't reliably manufactured.","updated":1788419688518,"created":1788419688518,"tags":["meta","photography","scientific-plate","scale","constraints"],"vendor_approved":false,"vendor":"","approved_on":"","custom":{"vendor_approved":false,"vendor":"","approved_on":""},"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":"vault"},"contentHash":"f4adcda4184110c5ab47a6345f076917","links":[{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.meta","alias":"meta","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.meta"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.photography","alias":"photography","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.photography"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.scientific-plate","alias":"scientific-plate","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.scientific-plate"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.scale","alias":"scale","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.scale"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.forensic-evidence-scales","id":"605332d0-02ad-4b4c-a636-10a9e9bfd8f0","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.constraints","alias":"constraints","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.constraints"}}],"anchors":{"the-problem":{"type":"header","text":"The problem","value":"the-problem","line":19,"column":0,"depth":2},"what-they-did":{"type":"header","text":"What they did","value":"what-they-did","line":27,"column":0,"depth":2},"what-we-take":{"type":"header","text":"What we take","value":"what-we-take","line":40,"column":0,"depth":2}},"children":[],"parent":"9fb155f7-93b1-42c9-9ca5-965ead6264cc","data":{}},"body":"<h1 id=\"forensic-evidence-photography--reference-scales\">Forensic evidence photography — reference scales<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#forensic-evidence-photography--reference-scales\"></a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"the-problem\">The problem<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#the-problem\"></a></h2>\n<p>Evidence photographs sometimes stand in a courtroom years after the object\nitself has moved, degraded, or been consumed by testing. A photograph that\nrecords only appearance and not true dimension can be challenged, or worse,\ncan misrepresent an object's actual size in a way nobody catches until\nit's too late to matter.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-they-did\">What they did<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#what-they-did\"></a></h2>\n<p>Forensic photography protocols call for a dimensional reference scale — the\nABFO No. 2 is a widely recognised example, an L-shaped ruler placed directly\nin frame alongside the evidence — so every photograph carries its own proof\nof scale rather than relying on a caption or a separate measurement log.\nStandard practice is to shoot the same subject both with and without the\nscale in frame, so the unobstructed record and the measurable record both\nexist. A NIST-adjacent survey of commercially available versions of that\nscale, however, found real inconsistency in how accurately different\nmanufacturers actually produced it — the standard exists, but conformance\nto it isn't guaranteed just because a scale is present in the photo.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-we-take\">What we take<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#what-we-take\"></a></h2>\n<p>Two things, in tension. The \"shoot it twice, with and without the scale\"\nconvention is worth adopting directly — it keeps the plain documentary\nimage and the measurable image from competing inside the same frame. The\nNIST finding is the more important lesson: a scale object in frame is only\nas trustworthy as the object itself, so if we adopt a physical reference\nscale across the exhibition, we should verify our own copies against a\nknown standard rather than assume any purchased ruler is accurate. That's\na small, cheap check that protects the credibility the whole \"declared\nscale\" rule is supposed to buy us.</p>\n<p>What doesn't transfer: forensic photography is built around chain-of-custody\nand courtroom admissibility requirements we don't have — we can borrow the\nscale convention without adopting the full evidentiary protocol around it.</p>\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https://www.ojp.gov/pdffiles1/nij/grants/243213.pdf\">https://www.ojp.gov/pdffiles1/nij/grants/243213.pdf</a></p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"tags\">Tags<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#tags\"></a></h2>\n<ol>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">meta (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">photography (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">scientific-plate (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">scale (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">constraints (Private)</a></li>\n</ol>","noteIndex":{"id":"28a6a50b-4c15-4c7d-b603-5a1d12809f1c","title":"Notes","desc":"Ideas in my o